Cyril Slobin wrote:
>"Dream filter"? What does it mean?

In English it's called a "dreamcatcher".  It's a net-like object, with
some decorative value.  It is traditionally hung near a bed and is alleged
to catch bad dreams so that they will not reach a sleeping person.  See

	http://freespace.virgin.net/derek.berger/dreamcatcher.html
	http://web.onramp.ca/rivernen/build_dc.htm

Regrettably, Google searches show mostly pages about the film and book
named "Dreamcatcher".  Wikipedia also lacks a proper entry, which I
shall now attempt to remedy.

